    "created_at": "2026-09-17T20:58:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-17T21:01:49Z",
    "body": "I currently:\n\n- connectedCallback create mutation observer for childList (actually, more accurately, I have a flat tree childList observer, which is the true thing that should always be observed, otherwise user composition won't work as expected)\n- then any time (flat) children change I handle the new picture. Ofc that's not as efficient if some later child is added (because parsing) that requires undoing or redoing previous work.\n\nA `connectedParsedCallback` would be nifty to avoid work until parsing is done, but we probably also need a way to know when we get connected without parsing.\n\nFor example, if connectedCallback took an argument like isParsing, or elements had a new property, which would be false if the element got connected from parsing, then we would know when to do work.\n\nTwo cases:\n\n- do work in connectedCallback (isParsing is false), we don't need to also wait for connectedParsedCallback or similar\n- skip connectedCallback (isParsing was true) and instead do work in connectedParsedCallback\n\nIf an element is disconnected before parsing finishes, connectedParsedCallback won't be called.\n\nWe cannot rely _only_ on something like connectedParsedCallback because an element can be appended with parent.append(el), so we need to know if isParsing is true or not when connected.\n\nMaybe a property makes sense (not arg to connectedCallback), so it also applies during `constructor`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
